WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:04.200
Where did you go this time, Riptoes? Yay!

00:00:06.760 --> 00:00:08.640
Look at all those plants!

00:00:09.280 --> 00:00:11.110
They're growing a lot of food.

00:00:11.900 --> 00:00:13.380
It's the late 1920s.

00:00:14.120 --> 00:00:15.320
These are crops,

00:00:15.620 --> 00:00:19.855
plants that farmers grow. They eat
some and sell the rest to earn money.

00:00:20.280 --> 00:00:21.480
Then a drought came.

00:00:22.120 --> 00:00:24.480
A drought is a long time without rain.

00:00:25.020 --> 00:00:26.890
The soil dried up and cracked.

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:31.020
Wind blew the dry soil
into giant dust storms.

00:00:32.040 --> 00:00:34.805
That's why people call
this area the Dust Bowl.

00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:40.540
Crops couldn't grow in dust, so families
packed up and moved west to find new

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:41.780
homes and jobs.

00:00:43.180 --> 00:00:46.415
Why do you think families
decided to leave their farms?

00:00:48.680 --> 00:00:54.629
Their crops couldn't grow anymore, so they
needed to find a new place to live and

00:00:54.629 --> 00:00:55.920
work. That's right.

00:00:56.900 --> 00:00:59.959
Families left to find places
where crops could grow.

00:01:00.780 --> 00:01:03.890
People learned an important
lesson from the Dust Bowl.

00:01:04.300 --> 00:01:09.090
Grass and plant roots hold soil in
place, like fingers gripping the ground.

00:01:09.860 --> 00:01:11.960
Now farmers plant cover crops,

00:01:12.660 --> 00:01:15.601
extra plants that cover
the ground and protect it.

00:01:15.900 --> 00:01:20.060
Their roots hold the soil down
tight, so wind can't blow it away.

00:01:21.060 --> 00:01:25.472
And scientists watch the weather and
warn farmers when a drought is coming.

00:01:25.700 --> 00:01:27.740
That way, everyone can get ready.

00:01:29.140 --> 00:01:32.022
The Dust Bowl was really
hard for those families.

00:01:32.180 --> 00:01:33.768
But people learned from it.

00:01:33.860 --> 00:01:36.507
Now they know how to
take care of their land.

00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:40.000
Planting grass and cover
crops keeps the soil safe.

00:01:40.240 --> 00:01:42.976
What would you like to
grow in your own garden?
